# OP-205 `a2a submit`: CC-002 — a `from`-mismatch is refused LOCALLY,
# before any mirror clone / network call (AC-201.3 ordering, config-only
# guard). This is the one write-path verb this package's exec'd-binary
# scripts CAN exercise end to end: the refusal happens before wire.go ever
# builds a GitHubHost or calls parseGitHubRepo.
mkdir .a2a/staging
cp foreign.md .a2a/staging/foreign.md
! exec a2a submit .a2a/staging/foreign.md
stderr 'CC-002'

# no-silent-yes-2026-08/P3 stage 2 (spec 03 §8 AC 4/13, DECISIONS.md § D9):
# a `classification: restricted` artifact is refused LOCALLY too, before
# any network call — like CC-002 above, this is a resolver-independent-of-
# the-host check, reached once the local mirror clone (already populated
# by this suite's own Setup) resolves. This fixture space carries THREE
# ACTIVE participants (axon/beta/gamma, fixOriginManifest) and the draft is
# from=axon/to=[beta], so gamma sits outside {from} u to — AC 4's own
# audience-exceeds scenario, for real.
#
# THIS ASSERTION CHANGED ON 2026-08-27 AND THE CHANGE IS THE POINT. It was
# written naming POL-025 (D9's capability-miss half) because at the time no
# concrete Resolver implemented ActiveParticipantLister, so `restricted`
# refused on the capability miss BEFORE the audience comparison it means to
# exercise was ever reached. The wave-1 fix wired that capability into both
# internal/cli's and internal/mcp's MirrorResolver, so the comparison is now
# reached and this path refuses with POL-024 — the true audience-exceeds rule
# plan/10-security.md §10.4 already declared normative and the validator did
# not enforce. The gate found the change; nobody had to remember to come back.
cp restricted.md .a2a/staging/restricted.md
! exec a2a submit .a2a/staging/restricted.md
stderr 'POL-024'

